.\" Man page for flow(1)
.\" Generated from COMPLETE_CLI_OPTIONS_AND_ARGUMENTS.md and SUMMARY_OF_AVAILABLE_OPTIONS.md
.TH FLOW 1 "November 2026" "ETL Madness Flow 1.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flow \- ETL pipeline execution engine, validator, visual builder server, and repository manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flow
.RI [ options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flow
(compiled from
.BR go-flow )
is the primary executable in the ETL Madness Flow ecosystem.
It executes XML-defined ETL and data workflow pipelines, runs preflight and schema/AST validations, starts an interactive local HTMX web server for visual pipeline authoring, transforms pipeline definitions via XSLT with auto-generated Mermaid workflow diagrams, and imports or exports pipelines, options profiles, and variable configurations across SQLite and external relational databases.
.PP
For the complete XML pipeline language specification (elements, attributes, control flow, database pools, and task types), see
.BR flow-pipeline (5).
.SH OPTIONS
Flags accept single-dash Go flag syntax (for example,
.B \-file
or
.BR \-\-file ).
Explicit command-line flags always take precedence over defaults loaded via
.BR \-options .
.SS Execution Options
.TP
.BI \-file " path|uri"
Path or URI to the XML file containing scripts, databases, and workflow nodes.
Supports local file paths, HTTP/HTTPS URLs, and
.B sql://
or
.B db://
database queries.
Default:
.IR scripts.xml .
.TP
.BI \-options " path|uri"
Path or URI to an XML CLI options defaults file
.RB ( <flow_cli_options><options>... ).
Values in this file set flag defaults without overriding flags explicitly passed on the command line.
.TP
.BI \-config " path|uri"
Optional path or URI to a
.I CONFIG.xml
file containing variable and database connection overrides, merged hierarchically with the base pipeline file.
.TP
.BI \-format " format"
Output formatting applied to execution results.
Supported values:
.B csv
(default),
.BR text ,
.BR json ,
.B jsonpretty
(or
.BR prettyjson ),
.B markdown
(or
.BR md ,
.BR table ),
and
.BR stream .
.TP
.BI \-vars " key=value[,key=value...]"
Comma-separated runtime variable overrides (for example,
.BR "\-vars \(dqTargetTable=tbl_prod,Threshold=500\(dq" ).
Recursively expands
.B {{var}}
placeholders up to 3 levels deep.
.SS Validation Options
.TP
.B \-validate
Validate XML schema (using XSD if
.B \-xsd
is specified) and AST semantic structure without executing any pipeline nodes.
Exits with status
.B 0
on success.
.TP
.B \-preflight
Execute preflight validation nodes only
.RB ( <preflight>
section), skipping the main pipeline
.B <flow>
nodes.
.TP
.BI \-xsd " path"
Path to an XML Schema Definition
.RI ( .xsd )
file used to validate the pipeline XML via
.B xmllint
prior to parsing.
.SS Diagnostic & Runtime Options
.TP
.B \-node-output
When logging to a database
.RB ( log_db ),
persist each node's execution output
.RB ( ResultsString
with automatic credential redaction) to the
.I node_output
column on
.I node.finished
rows in
.IR pipeline_events .
Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-debug
Enable verbose console logging, including connection string resolution, driver dialect detection, digital signature verification metadata, and sink telemetry.
.TP
.BI \-gopath " dir"
GOPATH directory for dynamic package imports used by the embedded Yaegi Go interpreter engine.
Defaults to the host
.B GOPATH
environment variable.
.SS Visualization Options
.TP
.BI \-xslt " path"
Path to a custom XSLT stylesheet.
Transforms pipeline XML while injecting an auto-generated Mermaid workflow diagram and exits immediately after transformation.
.TP
.BI \-out " path"
Output file path for XSLT-transformed XML produced by
.BR \-xslt .
.SS Security, Encryption & Signature Options
.TP
.B \-encrypted
Indicate that input files or database resources are AES-256-GCM encrypted and must be decrypted prior to parsing, or instruct
.B \-export-file
/
.B \-import-file
to encrypt output.
.TP
.BI \-secure-key " key"
Symmetric encryption or decryption key/passphrase.
Emits a security warning to
.I stderr
because command-line arguments are visible in process listings; prefer
.B \-key-file
or
.BR FLOW_SECURE_KEY .
.TP
.BI \-key-file " path"
Path to a protected file containing the symmetric key/passphrase.
Preferred over
.B \-secure-key
to avoid exposing secrets in system process tables.
.TP
.B \-verify-signature
Enforce digital signature verification before decrypting or executing the pipeline.
.TP
.BI \-public-key " path"
Path to a PEM-encoded public key file (RSA, ECDSA, or Ed25519) for digital signature verification.
.TP
.BI \-cert " path"
Path to an X.509 certificate file (PEM or DER format) for PKCS#7/CMS or X.509 RSA/ECDSA signature verification.
.TP
.BI \-ca-cert " path"
Path to a root or intermediate CA certificate file for signature verification certificate chain validation.
.TP
.BI \-keyring " path"
Path to an OpenPGP armored public keyring file for GPG signature verification.
.TP
.BI \-signature " path"
Path to a detached digital signature file
.RI ( .sig ,
.IR .asc ,
or
.IR .p7s ).
When omitted, companion files with matching basenames are checked automatically.
.SS Visual Builder UI Options
.TP
.B \-builder
Start the interactive local HTMX visual pipeline builder web server.
.TP
.BI \-builder-port " port"
TCP port for the visual builder web server.
Default
.B 0
selects an ephemeral dynamic port.
Can also be configured via
.B FLOW_BUILDER_PORT
or
.BR PORT .
.TP
.BI \-builder-db " path"
SQLite database file path used for visual builder local project storage.
Default:
.IR flow_builder.db .
.TP
.B \-purge-db
Purge all pipeline data from the SQLite visual builder database, re-initialize default records, and exit.
.SS Repository Import & Export Options
.TP
.BI \-import-file " path|uri"
Path or URI to a pipeline, options, or config XML file to import into the SQLite builder database or an external database specified by
.BR \-dsn .
.TP
.BI \-import-name " name"
Custom record name for the item imported with
.BR \-import-file .
Defaults to the source file basename without extension.
.TP
.BI \-import-type " type"
Item type for
.BR \-import-file :
.B pipeline
(default),
.BR options ,
or
.BR config .
.TP
.BI \-export-file " path"
Destination file path to export a pipeline, options, or config file, or
.B \-
for standard output
.RI ( stdout ).
Files written to disk use
.B 0600
permissions.
.TP
.BI \-export-name " name"
Name of the pipeline, options, or config record to export from the database (required when
.B \-export-file
is specified).
.TP
.BI \-export-type " type"
Item type for
.BR \-export-file :
.B pipeline
(default),
.BR options ,
or
.BR config .
.TP
.BI \-dsn " dsn"
External database DSN for direct repository import and export (supports
.BR sqlserver ,
.BR postgres ,
.BR mysql ,
and
.BR sqlite ).
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
The
.B \-format
flag accepts the following values:
.TP
.B csv
(Default) Standard comma-separated table displaying
.IR ScriptID ,
.IR ReturnCode ,
.IR Duration ,
and
.IR ResultsString .
.TP
.B text
Human-readable plain-text tabular format.
.TP
.B json
Compact JSON array containing all
.I ScriptResult
objects.
.TP
.BR jsonpretty ", " prettyjson
Formatted multi-line JSON with 4-space indentation.
.TP
.BR markdown ", " md ", " table
GitHub Flavored Markdown table.
.TP
.B stream
Real-time console event streaming mode with live node transitions, parent/child execution relationships, and audit sink telemetry.
.SH RESOURCE URIS
Arguments that load resources
.RB ( \-file ,
.BR \-options ,
.BR \-config ,
.BR \-import-file )
support uniform URI resolution:
.TP
.B Local File
Relative or absolute filesystem path, e.g.,
.IR ./pipelines/finance.xml .
.TP
.B HTTP / HTTPS
.I http://...
or
.IR https://...
.TP
.B HTTP Basic Auth
.I https://Basic%20<base64>@host/path/etl.xml
.TP
.B SQL Server Lookup
.I sql://sqlserver@<dsn>#table=<schema.table>[&column=<xml_col>][&name=<val>|&id=<val>]
.TP
.B Generic DB Alias
.I db://<driver>@<dsn>#table=<schema.table>&column=<xml_col>&key_col=<col>&key=<val>
(for example,
.IR "db://postgres@{{PG_USER}}:{{PG_PASSWORD}}@db:5432/app#table=flow_pipelines&column=pipeline_xml&key_col=name&key=BILLING" ).
.SH SECRET RESOLUTION PRECEDENCE
When encrypting or decrypting resources, passphrases and keys are resolved in the following order:
.IP 1. 4
.BI \-key-file " path"
(safest: reads key directly from a permission-restricted file).
.IP 2. 4
.BI \-secure-key " key"
(emits warning: command-line flags are visible in process listings such as
.BR ps (1)).
.IP 3. 4
XML options profile
.B <secure-key>
element (loaded via
.BR \-options ).
.IP 4. 4
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
environment variable.
.IP 5. 4
.B SECURE_KEY
fallback environment variable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
Primary symmetric passphrase used to decrypt or encrypt scripts, options, and configs.
.TP
.B SECURE_KEY
Secondary fallback symmetric passphrase if
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
is unset.
.TP
.B FLOW_BUILDER_PORT
Default TCP port for the HTMX visual builder web server when
.B \-builder-port
is not passed.
.TP
.B PORT
Generic fallback TCP port for the builder web server.
.TP
.B GOPATH
Go workspace directory used by Yaegi to import packages in interpreted blocks.
.TP
.BR USER ", " USERNAME
Captured for execution audit logs in
.IR pipeline_runs .
.TP
.BR HOSTNAME ", " COMPUTERNAME
Captured for execution audit logs in
.IR pipeline_runs .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/flow/share/xsd/pipeline.xsd
XML Schema Definition for
.B <pipeline>
files.
.TP
.I /opt/flow/share/xsd/options.xsd
XML Schema Definition for
.B \-options
CLI profile files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (pipeline ran successfully, schema/AST valid, signature verified, or import/export completed).
.TP
.B 1
Failure (execution error, validation failure, signature verification failure, missing/invalid decryption key, or database error).
.SH EXAMPLES
Execute a pipeline and render results as a Markdown table:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flow \-file ./pipelines/nightly_billing.xml \-format markdown
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate XSD schema and semantic AST without executing nodes:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flow \-file ./pipelines/etl.xml \-xsd /opt/flow/share/xsd/pipeline.xsd \-validate
.fi
.RE
.PP
Execute a signed and encrypted pipeline directly from a SQL repository:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flow \\
  \-file "sql://sqlserver@db:1433?database=ETL#table=dbo.flow_pipeline_content&name=NIGHTLY_SYNC" \\
  \-public-key /etc/flow/release_pub.pem \\
  \-key-file /etc/flow/master.key
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start the local visual pipeline builder UI on port 8080:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
flow \-builder \-builder-port 8080 \-builder-db ./builder_workspace.db
.fi
.RE
